    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d310ccf5_21bba7c0",
        "filename": "driver/ioexpander_it8801.c",
        "patchSetId": 23
      },
      "lineNbr": 115,
      "author": {
        "id": 1113904
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-08-19T22:10:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I know there\u0027s been a lot of bikeshedding over how this is overridable, but is there even a good reason we should have it overridable?\n\nWould it be a bad idea to just hardcode it?\n\nIt\u0027s getting quite interesting now since a lot of IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_KEYBOARD_COL2_INVERTED) also need to check what kso_mapping[2] is set to and configure the appropriate gpio instead. It would be easier if we could just assume this is always the same.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 115,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 115,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "17c575f9371d055e2bbcfcb46d9c00d5f7c7faa3",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e757595d_38927983",
        "filename": "driver/ioexpander_it8801.c",
        "patchSetId": 23
      },
      "lineNbr": 115,
      "author": {
        "id": 1273969
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-08-20T08:27:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is mainly for developer to declare kso pins testing or verifying in board.c",
      "parentUuid": "d310ccf5_21bba7c0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 115,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 115,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "17c575f9371d055e2bbcfcb46d9c00d5f7c7faa3",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "82863a76_18f876f1",
        "filename": "driver/ioexpander_it8801.c",
        "patchSetId": 23
      },
      "lineNbr": 115,
      "author": {
        "id": 1113904
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-08-20T23:00:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But my question is why would anyone change it in board.c? It seems we spent quite a bit of time testing this particular configuration, you lose all of that once you override it with a custom one.\n\nThe custom stuff, assuming inverted row2, will also need to use KSO20 as KSO2, since keyboard_raw_drive_column is already hardcoded to do that.\n\nWithout decoupling that too, it seems the __override is an future expansion thing that\u0027s not really complete. I\u0027m thinking https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/You_aren%27t_gonna_need_it",
      "parentUuid": "e757595d_38927983",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 115,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 115,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "17c575f9371d055e2bbcfcb46d9c00d5f7c7faa3",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
